    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: The Seven Eras of Marketing (Timeline Analysis)\n\nDescription:\n\nMarketing hasn't always been about Instagram likes and Super Bowl commercials. It has evolved over centuries, changing as technology and society changed. To understand where we are going, we must look at where we started.\n\nThe Task:\n\nUsing the class slides, create a summary of the Seven Eras of Marketing.\n\nPart 1: The Timeline\n\nFor each of the eras below, identify the Time Period and the Primary Focus (1 sentence per era).\n\n- Trade Era\n- Production Era\n- Selling Era\n- Marketing Department Era\n- Marketing Company Era\n- Relationship Marketing\n- Collaboration Era\n\nPart 2: The Shift\n\nExplain the difference between the Selling Era and the Marketing Company Era.\n\n- *Hint: In the Selling Era, businesses tried to trick people into buying. In the Marketing Era, businesses tried to... what?*\n\nPart 3: The Future (Critical Thinking)\n\nBased on what you see with AI, Virtual Reality, and privacy laws, write a 3-sentence prediction for what the *next* Era of Marketing will be called.\nPart 4: The Functions: Name the seven functions of marketing. Pick two and give a sports or entertainment example of each.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain how marketing has changed over time by giving the time period and main focus of each of the seven eras, from Trade to Collaboration (required)\n- I can describe the seven functions of marketing by naming all seven and showing two at work with real sports or entertainment examples\n- I can explain the marketing concept by comparing the Selling Era with the Marketing Company Era and saying what businesses started doing for customers instead of tricking them\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can think about the big picture by explaining in my prediction how AI, virtual reality, or privacy laws could change how businesses treat the people they market to\n- I can connect marketing's past to its future by linking my timeline and next-era prediction to how sports or entertainment marketing has changed and might change next\n- I can analyze trends by using at least one real trend, such as AI, virtual reality, or privacy laws, to back up my prediction and next-era name\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your responses as a Text Entry or File Upload.",
