    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L01 EVOLUTION OF MARKETING (FROM TRADE TO TIKTOK)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-39, 8175-43, 8175-41\n\nTHE TASK (what the student was asked to do)\nTitle: Assignment: The Seven Eras of Marketing (Timeline Analysis)\n\nDescription:\n\nMarketing hasn't always been about Instagram likes and Super Bowl commercials. It has evolved over centuries, changing as technology and society changed. To understand where we are going, we must look at where we started.\n\nThe Task:\n\nUsing the class slides, create a summary of the Seven Eras of Marketing.\n\nPart 1: The Timeline\n\nFor each of the eras below, identify the Time Period and the Primary Focus (1 sentence per era).\n\n- Trade Era\n- Production Era\n- Selling Era\n- Marketing Department Era\n- Marketing Company Era\n- Relationship Marketing\n- Collaboration Era\n\nPart 2: The Shift\n\nExplain the difference between the Selling Era and the Marketing Company Era.\n\n- *Hint: In the Selling Era, businesses tried to trick people into buying. In the Marketing Era, businesses tried to... what?*\n\nPart 3: The Future (Critical Thinking)\n\nBased on what you see with AI, Virtual Reality, and privacy laws, write a 3-sentence prediction for what the *next* Era of Marketing will be called.\nPart 4: The Functions: Name the seven functions of marketing. Pick two and give a sports or entertainment example of each.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain how marketing has changed over time by giving the time period and main focus of each of the seven eras, from Trade to Collaboration (required)\n- I can describe the seven functions of marketing by naming all seven and showing two at work with real sports or entertainment examples\n- I can explain the marketing concept by comparing the Selling Era with the Marketing Company Era and saying what businesses started doing for customers instead of tricking them\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can think about the big picture by explaining in my prediction how AI, virtual reality, or privacy laws could change how businesses treat the people they market to\n- I can connect marketing's past to its future by linking my timeline and next-era prediction to how sports or entertainment marketing has changed and might change next\n- I can analyze trends by using at least one real trend, such as AI, virtual reality, or privacy laws, to back up my prediction and next-era name\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your responses as a Text Entry or File Upload.\n\nPRIMARY COMPETENCY (Milestone 1; must be MET)\n- 8175-39 Explain marketing as it relates to the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * a general definition of the term marketing\n    * the primary function of marketing (i.e., generating revenue)\n    * examples illustrating the role of marketing in the sports, entertainment, and event industries\n\nSECONDARY COMPETENCIES (must be at least PARTIALLY MET)\n- 8175-43 Describe the marketing functions.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * a definition of the functions\n    * selling\n    * distribution (channel management)\n    * product/service management\n    * promotion\n    * pricing\n    * financing\n    * marketing information management (MIM)\n    * market planning\n    * an explanation of how each function relates to the sports, entertainment, and event industries\n- 8175-41 Describe the marketing concept as related to the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * identifying customers\n    * recognizing customer wants and needs\n    * satisfying diverse and changing customer wants and needs\n    * earning a return on investment (ROI) and managing spend (i.e., money allocated for marketing activities [e.g., costs])\n\nTERTIARY COMPETENCIES (never required; name any the work clearly shows under ALSO SHOWN)\n- 8175-11 Demonstrate big-picture thinking.\n- 8175-45 Describe the past, present, and future of the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n- 8175-47 Analyze trends and innovations in the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nCheck the \"Future Prediction\" section.\n\n- Eras: Did they list the 7 eras correctly?\n- Prediction: Did they offer a thoughtful idea for the \"Next Era\"?\n\nPASSING RULE: APPROVED when Milestone 1 (the primary competency) is MET and Milestones 2, 3 and 4 are each MET or PARTIALLY MET. Tertiary competencies never affect the result.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work does every part of the task the assignment asks for, in the student's own words. Specific examples, not general statements. Judge each competency only by what this assignment asks the student to do. The lines under a competency are examples of what evidence can look like, not a checklist: one specific, well-done example that fits the task is enough, and a part of a competency the task does not ask for is never required."
