    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L02 INTRINSIC MOTIVATION (THE PASSION TEST)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-107, 8175-3\n\nTHE TASK (what the student was asked to do)\nTitle: Assignment: The Passion Test (Intrinsic Motivation)\n\nDescription:\n\nTo be successful in a high energy field like Sports and Entertainment Marketing, you need \"drive.\" But drive comes from two places: Extrinsic Motivation (money, grades, rewards) and Intrinsic Motivation (doing something because you love it). The most successful people build careers around things they are inherently motivated to do.\n\nThe Task:\n\nPlease answer the following question in 2 to 3 sentences:\n\nWhat is something that you do because you are inherently motivated to do it?\n\n- It can be related to any of your interests (sports, art, coding, organizing, helping people), but please keep it school appropriate.\n- Explain *why* you enjoy it.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can identify a personal interest that drives me by naming one thing I do because I love it and explaining in 2 to 3 sentences why I enjoy it (required)\n- I can explain what drives me by showing that I keep doing this thing on my own, without money, rewards, or anyone pushing me, and saying what keeps me going\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your response as a Text Entry.\n\nPRIMARY COMPETENCY (Milestone 1; must be MET)\n- 8175-107 Identify personal skills and interests applicable to the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * individual personal skills (e.g., leadership ability, problem-solving ability, organizational ability)\n    * interests (e.g., sports, theater, music, physical fitness, recreational activities, volunteer activities)\n    * networking with local business representatives\n    * volunteering or working in sports, entertainment, and event industries to gauge one’s interest in the business of sports, entertainment, and events and to gain valuable work experience\n\nSECONDARY COMPETENCIES (must be at least PARTIALLY MET)\n- 8175-3 Demonstrate initiative and self-direction.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * recognizing the importance of proactive, independent decision making\n    * identifying workplace needs\n    * completing tasks with minimal direct supervision\n    * applying solutions\n\nTERTIARY COMPETENCIES (never required; name any the work clearly shows under ALSO SHOWN)\n- None for this assignment.\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nThis is a participation grade.\n\n- Did they answer the question?\n- Is it school appropriate?\n\nPASSING RULE: APPROVED when Milestone 1 (the primary competency) is MET and Milestones 2, 3 and 4 are each MET or PARTIALLY MET. Tertiary competencies never affect the result.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work does every part of the task the assignment asks for, in the student's own words. Specific examples, not general statements. Judge each competency only by what this assignment asks the student to do. The lines under a competency are examples of what evidence can look like, not a checklist: one specific, well-done example that fits the task is enough, and a part of a competency the task does not ask for is never required."
