    "promptText": "Title: Discussion: Ethical Dilemmas in the Workplace\n\nDescription:\n\nIn the business world, the \"right answer\" is not always easy to find. Ethical leaders cannot stand back and let unethical behavior take place.\n\nThe Task:\n\n- Select: Pick one of the four scenarios below.\n- Post: Tell us which scenario you chose. Then, outline how you would react. Be sure to maintain professionalism in your planned response.\n- Reply: Once you have posted your response, reply to two of your classmates.\n\nScenario 1: The Server\n\nOverhearing coworkers making derogatory comments about customers. Do you confront them?\n\nScenario 2: The Hiring Manager\n\nConsidering hiring a qualified friend. Is this favoritism?\n\nScenario 3: The Treasurer\n\nAsked to fudge numbers in the budget to cover costs. Everyone else agrees. What do you do?\n\nScenario 4: The Bystander\n\nWitnessing intimidation of a younger student in the hallway. How do you intervene?\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can act with integrity by naming my scenario and outlining exactly what I would do to act honestly and fairly even when it is hard (required)\n- I can identify unethical business practices by naming what is unethical in my scenario and explaining why it is wrong, not just against the rules\n- I can act professionally by writing my planned response in a calm, respectful tone I could really use at work, without insults or slang\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can resolve conflict by explaining how I would handle the people in my scenario so the problem gets solved without making the conflict worse\n- I can explain how communication shapes work relationships by saying what I would tell the people in my scenario and how saying it that way protects our relationship\n\nSubmission:\n\nPost your initial response and two replies in the Discussion Board.",
