    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: What IS Branding? (The Mentor Challenge)\n\nDescription:\n\nWe have spent the year looking at logos, slogans, and the emotional connections companies make with consumers. Now, it is time to synthesize that information.\n\nThe Scenario:\n\nImagine that a younger student, or perhaps a relative with absolutely no business background, comes up to you and asks: \"I keep hearing people talk about 'branding,' but I don't get it. What actually IS branding?\"\n\nThe Task:\n\nStep into the role of the teacher. Write out your response to this person (Minimum 250 words).\n\nStructure:\n\n- The Introduction: Start by telling them what branding is not. Define it simply.\n- The Examples: Use a real example (like Apple or Coca Cola). Explain *why* people buy that brand.\n- The Promise: Explain how a brand is a promise to the customer. That trust is branding.\n- The Conclusion: Wrap it up by telling them why it matters.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain branding by saying what it is not, defining it simply, explaining why people buy a real brand like Apple, and showing how a brand is a promise (required)\n- I can translate business language into everyday words by explaining branding so someone with no business background understands it, including any business term I use\n- I can write a clear explanation of at least 250 words with an introduction, an example, the promise, and a conclusion, checked for spelling and grammar\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can think critically about brands by explaining the real reasons people choose my example brand over others instead of only describing it\n- I can explain branding in sports, entertainment, or events by using an example from one of them to show how a brand builds trust with fans\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your response as a Text Entry.",
