    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Service Experience Reflection (The Gold Standard)\n\nDescription:\n\nIn marketing, we often focus on the product, but the *experience* is what keeps customers coming back. Great service can make a cheap product feel luxurious, while bad service can ruin even the best product.\n\nThe Task:\n\nThink of a time when you were impressed with the service you received from a company.\n\nPrompt:\n\nPlease write a reflection responding to the following questions. You must respond using at least 10 complete sentences.\n\n- The Action: What exactly did the employee or company do that made them stand out from their competitors?\n- The Emotion: How did it make you feel as a customer?\n- The Value: What does this do to the perceived value of your purchase?\n- The Recovery: Now think of a time service went wrong, for you or someone you know. Using the LAST steps from class, explain how the employee should have handled the complaint.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain why customer service matters by describing what a company did to stand out, how it made me feel, and how it changed the value of my purchase (required)\n- I can describe how to handle a customer complaint by using the LAST steps to explain how the employee should have handled a time service went wrong\n- I can write a clear reflection of at least 10 complete sentences that answers all four questions and is checked for spelling and grammar\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can recognize good customer service by naming the helpful, courteous, or knowledgeable actions that made the good service work and were missing when service went wrong\n- I can think about the big picture by explaining how great or bad service from one employee affects the whole company and whether customers come back\n- I can explain hospitality by showing how the way I was welcomed and treated as a guest shaped my whole experience, not just the product\n- I can compare types of customer interaction by saying what kind of service I got in each story, such as self-service or full service, and how it affected my experience\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your reflection as a Text Entry.",
