    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L11 CHHS BRAND AUDIT (INTERNAL ANALYSIS)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-57, 8175-42, 8175-59\n\nTHE TASK (what the student was asked to do)\nTitle: Assignment: CHHS Brand Audit (The Home Field Advantage)\n\nDescription:\n\nYou walk the halls every day, but have you ever looked at Clover Hill High School as a brand? Just like a sports team or a clothing line, our school has an image, a target audience, and a reputation.\n\nThe Task:\n\nConduct a brand audit of Clover Hill High School. Write a 250 word (minimum) essay covering the following three areas.\n\n1. Target Market Identification (Min. 75 words)\n\n- Who are we serving?\n- Identify the target market (Demographics and Psychographics).\n\n2. Brand Quality Assessment (Min. 100 words)\n\n- Assess the quality of the current \"Cavalier\" brand.\n- What do the logo, the colors, and the reputation say to the community?\n- Determine specific areas for improvement.\n\n3. Cultural and Societal Trends (Min. 75 words)\n\n- Analyze current cultural and societal trends that may impact rebranding efforts (e.g., social media, mental health awareness).\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can evaluate a school brand by explaining what the Cavalier logo, colors, and reputation say to the community and naming specific areas for improvement (required)\n- I can explain target marketing by identifying who Clover Hill High School serves using both demographics and psychographics in at least 75 words\n- I can explain reasons for rebranding by showing how current cultural and societal trends, such as social media or mental health awareness, could push the school to rebrand\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can write a clear essay of at least 250 words that meets the word count for each section and is checked for spelling and grammar\n- I can analyze trends by naming at least one current trend and explaining how it changes what students and the community expect from the school's brand\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your essay as a Text Entry.\n\nPRIMARY COMPETENCY (Milestone 1; must be MET)\n- 8175-57 Explain the concept of branding as it relates to sports, entertainment, and event marketing.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * the importance of brand development\n    * team vs. individual branding\n    * the importance of brands in product/service planning\n    * how brand names are generated\n    * branding strategies (e.g., brand extension, brand licensing, mixed brands, co-branding)\n    * stages or levels of brand recognition\n\nSECONDARY COMPETENCIES (must be at least PARTIALLY MET)\n- 8175-42 Explain the concept of target marketing.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * target marketing\n    * area of dominant influence (ADI)\n    * market segmentation\n    * customer persona\n    * addressing the importance of demographics, psychographics, geographics, and buying behaviors of local, state, and national markets as they relate to target markets in the sports, entertainment, and event industries\n- 8175-59 Explain the concept of and reasons for rebranding.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * new target market(s)\n    * company image and identification\n    * new product line\n    * altered public image\n    * new revenue potential\n    * changes in technology\n    * cultural or societal trends\n    * identification of brand quality and target market\n\nTERTIARY COMPETENCIES (never required; name any the work clearly shows under ALSO SHOWN)\n- 8175-21 Demonstrate reading and writing skills.\n- 8175-47 Analyze trends and innovations in the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nFocus assessment on Section 2 (Brand Quality). Read the student's critique carefully. If they utilize vocabulary words such as \"Target Market\" or \"Demographics\" correctly in context, award full credit.\n\nPASSING RULE: APPROVED when Milestone 1 (the primary competency) is MET and Milestones 2, 3 and 4 are each MET or PARTIALLY MET. Tertiary competencies never affect the result.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work does every part of the task the assignment asks for, in the student's own words. Specific examples, not general statements. Judge each competency only by what this assignment asks the student to do. The lines under a competency are examples of what evidence can look like, not a checklist: one specific, well-done example that fits the task is enough, and a part of a competency the task does not ask for is never required."
