    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L12 THE SWOT ANALYSIS (COMPANY EDITION)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-105, 8175-101\n\nTHE TASK (what the student was asked to do)\nTitle: Assignment: SWOT Analysis (The War Room)\n\nDescription:\n\nA SWOT Analysis is the foundation of any marketing plan. It helps businesses understand where they stand compared to the competition.\n\nThe Task:\n\nSelect a major Sports Team or Entertainment Company (e.g., The Commanders, Disney, Netflix). Complete a SWOT Analysis for them.\n\n1. Internal Factors (Inside the Building)\n\n- List 2 Strengths: (e.g., Loyal fan base, star player).\n- List 2 Weaknesses: (e.g., Old stadium, high ticket prices).\n\n2. External Factors (Outside the World)\n\n- List 2 Opportunities: (e.g., Expanding to international markets).\n- List 2 Threats: (e.g., Rising inflation, a new competitor).\n\n3. The Strategy\n\n- Based on your analysis, give one specific recommendation to the General Manager.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can analyze a team or company's position by naming 2 internal strengths, 2 weaknesses, 2 outside opportunities and 2 threats it faces (required)\n- I can explain competition by naming at least one real competitor or competing option in my analysis and explaining how it affects my team or company\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can plan a marketing move by giving the General Manager one specific recommendation and showing which parts of my SWOT analysis it comes from\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your analysis as a Text Entry.\n\nPRIMARY COMPETENCY (Milestone 1; must be MET)\n- 8175-105 Identify the components of a SWOT analysis.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * strengths\n    * weaknesses\n    * opportunities\n    * threats\n\nSECONDARY COMPETENCIES (must be at least PARTIALLY MET)\n- 8175-101 Explain competition as it relates to the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * direct competition\n    * indirect competition\n    * price competition\n    * non-price competition\n\nTERTIARY COMPETENCIES (never required; name any the work clearly shows under ALSO SHOWN)\n- 8175-102 Explain the components of the marketing plan.\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nCheck for the distinction between Internal and External.\n\n- Strengths/Weaknesses must be Internal.\n- Opportunities/Threats must be External.\n\nPASSING RULE: APPROVED when Milestone 1 (the primary competency) is MET and Milestones 2, 3 and 4 are each MET or PARTIALLY MET. Tertiary competencies never affect the result.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work does every part of the task the assignment asks for, in the student's own words. Specific examples, not general statements. Judge each competency only by what this assignment asks the student to do. The lines under a competency are examples of what evidence can look like, not a checklist: one specific, well-done example that fits the task is enough, and a part of a competency the task does not ask for is never required."
