    "promptText": "Title: Project: Local Business Deep Dive (The Consultant's Report)\n\nDescription:\n\nYou will act as a consultant analyzing a local business in the Sports and Entertainment industry (e.g., Movie Theaters, Bowling Alleys, Music Venues, Laser Tag).\n\nThe Task Overview:\n\n- Day 1: Research and Scripting: Select your business. Analyze their Brand, Product, and Offerings. Write a word-for-word Script.\n- Day 2: Slide Deck Creation: Use your script to create a slide deck. Follow best practices (Minimal text).\n- Day 3: Peer Feedback Loop: Present to a partner. Provide and receive feedback.\n- Day 4: The Pitch: Presentations are shared with the class.\n\nKey Analysis Points:\n\n- Brand Analysis: What is their reputation?\n- Future Forecast: What changes would you expect for this business in the next 5 years based on AI and trends?\n- Ownership: Is the business a sole proprietorship, partnership, corporation, LLC or franchise? How does that change who makes decisions and who takes the risk?\n- Behind the Scenes: In one or two sentences each, explain how the business plans, how it is managed, how it handles money, the skills its workers need, the technology it runs on, one labor issue, and one health, safety or environmental issue.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can compare types of business ownership by naming my business's ownership type and explaining how it changes who makes decisions and who takes the risk (required)\n- I can analyze trends by predicting at least one change for my business in the next 5 years and explaining which AI tool or trend would cause it\n- I can present like a consultant by building a minimal-text slide deck from my script and presenting it to the class\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can speak clearly to an audience by writing my word-for-word script so it sounds natural spoken aloud and is clear to my classmates\n- I can collaborate with a partner by using at least one piece of feedback from my Day 3 partner to improve my final presentation\n- I can use reliable information by basing my brand analysis on real facts about the business and saying where those facts came from\n- I can examine how a business plans by explaining in one or two sentences how my business plans ahead\n- I can examine how a business is managed by explaining in one or two sentences how my business is run\n- I can examine financial responsibility by explaining in one or two sentences how my business handles its money\n- I can identify the skills workers need by explaining in one or two sentences what my business's workers must be able to do in their jobs\n- I can explain the technology behind a business by describing in one or two sentences the technology my business runs on\n- I can examine labor issues by naming one labor issue my business faces and explaining it in one or two sentences\n- I can examine health, safety, and environmental issues by naming one my business faces and explaining it in one or two sentences\n- I can explain why the sports and entertainment industry matters by showing why my business matters to the people who go there and to the local community\n- I can explain how a sports or entertainment business works by showing how my business's brand, products, offerings, planning, management, and money fit together to keep it running\n- I can identify jobs in the industry by naming specific jobs at my business when I describe the skills its workers need\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your Script (Day 1) and Final Presentation (Day 4).",
