    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Olymponomics (The Economics of Hosting)\n\nDescription:\n\nHosting the Olympics is glamorous. It brings the eyes of the world to your city. But it also costs billions of dollars. Today, you are an economic analyst deciding if the \"glory\" is worth the \"price tag.\"\n\nThe Task:\n\nComplete the two parts below to determine if hosting is a smart play or a financial disaster.\n\nPart 1: The Research\n\nResearch the Economics of the Olympics. specifically looking for:\n\n- The Cost: How much does it cost?\n- The Revenue: How does the city make money back?\n- The White Elephants: What happened to stadiums in Athens or Rio after the games?\n- The Successes: Look up the 1984 Los Angeles Olympics.\n- The Economy: Was the host country's economy growing or in a recession at the time? How did that affect the results?\n\nPart 2: The Essay (200 Words)\n\nWrite a 200 word persuasive essay answering this prompt:\n\n*\"Based on economic data and historical examples, is hosting the Olympic Games a smart financial investment for a city, or a financial trap?\"*\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Evidence: Cite specific examples.\n- Citations: List at least 3 sources at the bottom.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain the economics of hosting the Olympics by arguing it is a smart investment or a trap, using the cost, the revenue, and what happened to the stadiums (required)\n- I can use sources well by listing at least 3 sources at the bottom of my essay and using specific facts from them as examples\n- I can write persuasively in a 200-word essay that states my position clearly, supports it with examples, and is checked for spelling and grammar\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can examine community issues by explaining how hosting affected the host city and its people, such as the empty stadiums in Athens or Rio\n- I can explain how the business cycle affects big events by saying whether the host country's economy was growing or in a recession and how that affected the Games' results\n- I can explain supply and demand by comparing demand for tickets, hotels, or stadiums during the Games with afterward and how that affected the city's money\n\nSubmission:\n\nType your essay in Google Docs, then paste the text into the submission box.",
