    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: The Ticketmaster Problem (Distribution Channels)\n\nDescription:\n\nDistribution is the process of getting the product to the customer. The path a ticket takes from the stadium to your phone involves \"Intermediaries\" (Middlemen), and each one charges a fee.\n\nThe Task:\n\nAnalyze the distribution channel of a major concert ticket.\n\n1. The Chain of Command\n\n- Identify the 3 parties involved in a standard ticket sale (The Producer, The Intermediary, The Consumer).\n\n2. The Venue Impact\n\n- Why does the Venue (Stadium vs. Club) matter for distribution?\n\n3. The Ethics of the \"Secondary Market\"\n\n- Scenario: A scalper uses a \"Bot\" to buy 100 tickets in 1 second, then resells them for double the price.\n- Question: Is this smart business (Supply and Demand) or unethical behavior? Should it be illegal?\n- Response: Write a 100 word opinion piece. Defend your stance.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain a distribution channel by identifying the producer, intermediary, and consumer in a concert ticket sale and each one's role in getting the ticket to the fan (required)\n- I can judge whether a business practice is ethical by taking a clear stand in my 100-word opinion piece on bot scalping and saying whether it should be illegal\n- I can identify distribution challenges by explaining why a stadium versus a club changes how tickets get to fans\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can explain supply and demand by using it to show why the scalper can resell tickets for double the price\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your analysis as a Text Entry.",
