    "promptText": "Title: Project: My Cause My Cleats (The Campaign Pitch)\n\nDescription:\n\nIt is your job to design the visuals and the strategy for the \"My Cause My Cleats\" campaign. You are not just designing a shoe; you are designing a message that needs to raise money and awareness.\n\nDeliverables:\n\nCreate a slide presentation (approx. 5 to 7 slides) that \"pitches\" your concept to the NFL.\n\n1. The Partners\n\n- Identify the Athlete and the Non Profit.\n- Explain the \"Why.\"\n\n2. The Strategy\n\n- Awareness: How will these cleats get attention?\n- Fundraising: Propose one specific idea to raise money.\n- The Promotion: Choose one sales promotion for your campaign (a giveaway, contest, coupon or limited-edition item) and give one advantage and one disadvantage of it.\n\n3. The Visuals\n\n- The Cleats: Insert a picture of your final cleat design.\n- The Merch: Create one promotional item that visually represents three brands at once: The Athlete, The Non Profit, and The NFL Team.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can plan a promotional campaign by explaining how my cleats will get attention, proposing one fundraising idea and picking a sales promotion that fits my athlete and non profit (required)\n- I can weigh the pros and cons of sales promotions by choosing one giveaway, contest, coupon or limited-edition item and giving one advantage and one disadvantage of it\n- I can create original ideas by designing my own cleats and one merch item that shows the athlete, the non profit and the NFL team at once\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can present a business idea clearly by pitching my concept to the NFL in about 5 to 7 slides, each covering one part of the plan\n- I can identify ways to get a campaign seen by naming the specific places or channels my campaign will use to get the cleats noticed\n- I can explain what a sponsorship or endorsement deal gives each side by showing what the athlete and the non profit each gain from their partnership\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your presentation file.",
