    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L22 MY CAUSE MY CLEATS (THE CAMPAIGN PITCH)\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-93, 8175-92, 8175-1\n\nTHE TASK (what the student was asked to do)\nTitle: Project: My Cause My Cleats (The Campaign Pitch)\n\nDescription:\n\nIt is your job to design the visuals and the strategy for the \"My Cause My Cleats\" campaign. You are not just designing a shoe; you are designing a message that needs to raise money and awareness.\n\nDeliverables:\n\nCreate a slide presentation (approx. 5 to 7 slides) that \"pitches\" your concept to the NFL.\n\n1. The Partners\n\n- Identify the Athlete and the Non Profit.\n- Explain the \"Why.\"\n\n2. The Strategy\n\n- Awareness: How will these cleats get attention?\n- Fundraising: Propose one specific idea to raise money.\n- The Promotion: Choose one sales promotion for your campaign (a giveaway, contest, coupon or limited-edition item) and give one advantage and one disadvantage of it.\n\n3. The Visuals\n\n- The Cleats: Insert a picture of your final cleat design.\n- The Merch: Create one promotional item that visually represents three brands at once: The Athlete, The Non Profit, and The NFL Team.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can plan a promotional campaign by explaining how my cleats will get attention, proposing one fundraising idea and picking a sales promotion that fits my athlete and non profit (required)\n- I can weigh the pros and cons of sales promotions by choosing one giveaway, contest, coupon or limited-edition item and giving one advantage and one disadvantage of it\n- I can create original ideas by designing my own cleats and one merch item that shows the athlete, the non profit and the NFL team at once\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can present a business idea clearly by pitching my concept to the NFL in about 5 to 7 slides, each covering one part of the plan\n- I can identify ways to get a campaign seen by naming the specific places or channels my campaign will use to get the cleats noticed\n- I can explain what a sponsorship or endorsement deal gives each side by showing what the athlete and the non profit each gain from their partnership\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your presentation file.\n\nPRIMARY COMPETENCY (Milestone 1; must be MET)\n- 8175-93 Describe the elements of sports, entertainment, and event promotional campaigns.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * event, product, or service\n    * campaign objectives\n    * target marketing\n    * campaign activities and schedule\n    * budget\n    * key performance indicators (KPI)\n\nSECONDARY COMPETENCIES (must be at least PARTIALLY MET)\n- 8175-92 Explain the advantages and disadvantages of using various forms of sales promotion in the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * the purpose and importance of sales promotion and marketing activities to stimulate purchasing and sales (e.g., contests, coupons, rebates, endorsements)\n    * trade promotions (e.g., trade shows, sales incentives)\n    * consumer sales promotions (e.g., licensing, visual merchandising)\n    * the importance of lead generation\n- 8175-1 Demonstrate creativity and innovation.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * discussing the importance of creativity and innovation in the workplace\n    * brainstorming and contributing ideas, strategies, and solutions\n    * developing and/or improving products, services, or processes\n    * identifying and allocating available resources\n\nTERTIARY COMPETENCIES (never required; name any the work clearly shows under ALSO SHOWN)\n- 8175-50 Develop presentation skills as a form of business communication.\n- 8175-74 Identify methods of communication used in sports, entertainment, and event promotion.\n- 8175-87 Explain sponsorship and endorsements as they relate to the sports, entertainment, and event industries.\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nUtilize a checklist approach.\n\n- Cleat design included?\n- Charity identified?\n- Fundraising idea included?\n\nPASSING RULE: APPROVED when Milestone 1 (the primary competency) is MET and Milestones 2, 3 and 4 are each MET or PARTIALLY MET. Tertiary competencies never affect the result.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work does every part of the task the assignment asks for, in the student's own words. Specific examples, not general statements. Judge each competency only by what this assignment asks the student to do. The lines under a competency are examples of what evidence can look like, not a checklist: one specific, well-done example that fits the task is enough, and a part of a competency the task does not ask for is never required."
