    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Sales Training Camp (Methods and Roleplay)\n\nDescription:\n\nThere are two main ways products are sold: Personal Selling and Non-Personal Selling. To be effective in business, you must understand the pros and cons of both.\n\nThe Task:\n\nComplete the three sections below based on the class lecture.\n\nPart 1: Methods of Selling Analysis\n\n- Personal Selling: Define it. List 2 Benefits and 2 Negatives.\n- Non-Personal Selling: Define it. List 2 Benefits and 2 Negatives.\n\nPart 2: The 6 Steps of a Sale\n\n- List the 6 Steps of the Selling Process in order.\n- Key Concept: Complete this sentence: \"Selling is __________.\"\n\nPart 3: The \"No, No, Yes\" Roleplay\n\n- Instructions: Get into groups of two. Act as Salesperson and Customer.\n- The Rule: The Customer must reject the Salesperson twice before saying \"Yes.\"\n- The Record: Write down what you sold, your opening line, the Customer's two rejections, what you said after each one, and the line that got the \"Yes.\"\n- Reflection: How did it feel to be rejected twice? Did you have to change your strategy?\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain the types of selling by defining personal and non-personal selling and listing 2 benefits and 2 negatives of each (required)\n- I can explain the selling process by listing its 6 steps in the right order and finishing the sentence \"Selling is ...\"\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can listen and respond in a sales conversation by recording what I sold, my opening line, the Customer's two rejections, my replies, and the line that won the \"Yes.\"\n- I can work with a partner by playing Salesperson and Customer, following the two-rejection rule, and reflecting on whether I had to change my strategy\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your responses as a Text Entry.",
