    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L25 BHM ENTREPRENEUR VALENTINE\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-15, 8175-1\n\nTHE TASK (what the student was asked to do)\nTitle: Extra Credit: Black History Month Entrepreneur Valentine\n\nDescription:\n\nFor this opportunity, you will explore the intersection of history and business by researching a Black entrepreneur who has made a significant impact on their industry.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Select a Subject: Choose one Black entrepreneur.\n- Conduct Research: Gather information regarding their background and business ventures.\n- Design a Card: Create a Valentine's Day card dedicated to them.\n- Content Integration: You must incorporate three specific facts into the card's design or text.\n\n- *Example:* \"Roses are red, violets are blue, you founded [Company Name] in 1992...\"\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can research a person using reliable information by putting three specific, accurate facts about one Black entrepreneur's background or business ventures into my card (required)\n- I can be creative by designing an original Valentine's Day card, with my own verse and layout, that works the three facts in\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can show respect for others' backgrounds by honoring my entrepreneur's background and impact on their industry with care in my card\n\nSubmission:\n\nUpload your final card design as a PDF or image file.\n\nPRIMARY COMPETENCY (Milestone 1; must be MET)\n- 8175-15 Demonstrate information-literacy skills.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * defining information literacy\n    * locating and evaluating credible and relevant sources of information\n    * using information effectively to accomplish work-related tasks\n\nSECONDARY COMPETENCIES (must be at least PARTIALLY MET)\n- 8175-1 Demonstrate creativity and innovation.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * discussing the importance of creativity and innovation in the workplace\n    * brainstorming and contributing ideas, strategies, and solutions\n    * developing and/or improving products, services, or processes\n    * identifying and allocating available resources\n\nTERTIARY COMPETENCIES (never required; name any the work clearly shows under ALSO SHOWN)\n- 8175-8 Demonstrate respect for diversity.\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nThis is designed as a quick check.\n\n- Did they include 3 facts?\n- Is it a card format?\n\nPASSING RULE: APPROVED when Milestone 1 (the primary competency) is MET and Milestones 2, 3 and 4 are each MET or PARTIALLY MET. Tertiary competencies never affect the result.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work does every part of the task the assignment asks for, in the student's own words. Specific examples, not general statements. Judge each competency only by what this assignment asks the student to do. The lines under a competency are examples of what evidence can look like, not a checklist: one specific, well-done example that fits the task is enough, and a part of a competency the task does not ask for is never required."
