    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Spring Break Field Report (Marketing in the Wild)\n\nDescription:\n\nYou have just spent a week away from school, but you were likely surrounded by business the entire time.\n\nThe Task:\n\nUsing at least 200 words, write a reflection on the marketing you encountered over Spring Break.\n\n1. The Observation (The What)\n\n- Tell me specific examples of marketing that you noticed (e.g., sponsored posts, billboards, movie trailers).\n\n2. The Reverse Engineering (The How)\n\n- Describe the processes that you imagine went into the development of this marketing campaign.\n- How did they get it from an idea to what you experienced? Who had to approve the budget? Who designed the graphics?\n- Keeping You: Did the brand try to keep you after the first ad (a follow, an email sign-up, a loyalty app, a discount code)? Explain how.\n- Was It Worth It: How could the company tell whether the campaign earned back what it cost?\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain promotion by giving specific marketing examples I noticed over Spring Break and describing how one campaign likely went from an idea to what I saw (required)\n- I can identify ways brands keep customers by explaining how one brand tried to keep me after the first ad, like a follow, email sign-up, loyalty app or discount code\n- I can explain why a campaign's return on investment matters by describing how the company could tell whether the campaign earned back what it cost\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can think critically by reasoning through who likely approved the budget and who designed the graphics, rather than only describing the ad\n- I can describe online marketing tools by naming the ones I ran into, such as sponsored posts, email sign-ups or loyalty apps, and saying how each worked\n- I can explain how brands pick platforms by saying why the brand chose the app, site or feed where I saw its ad to reach people like me\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your reflection as a Text Entry.",
