    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Designing Unbiased Surveys (Google Forms)\n\nDescription:\n\nWe are in the process of designing a new service. To do this successfully, we need to know what the customer wants. However, asking the wrong questions leads to wrong answers.\n\nThe Task:\n\n- Create: Open Google Forms and start a new blank form.\n- Design Questions: Create three survey questions.\n\n- Requirement A: Include two quantitative questions (Multiple Choice or Scale).\n- Requirement B: Include one qualitative question (Open-ended paragraph).\n\n- Bias Check: Review your questions. Do they suggest the \"correct\" answer? If so, rewrite them to be neutral.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can explain what market research is for by writing two quantitative questions and one qualitative question that would find out what customers want from the new service (required)\n- I can spot and fix bias by checking each question and explaining in one or two sentences which question I rewrote and what I changed to make it neutral\n- I can use Google Forms by building my three questions, with answer choices for the two quantitative ones, and pasting the form's send link\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can explain why research matters to a marketing plan by asking questions whose answers could actually help us decide how to design the new service\n\nSubmission:\n\nClick the \"Send\" button on your form, copy the link, and paste the URL as your submission.\n\nBelow the link, type your three questions exactly as they appear on the form, with the answer choices for the two quantitative questions. Then, in one or two sentences, say which question you rewrote after the Bias Check and what you changed.",
