    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: Survey Analysis (Data Driven Decisions)\n\nDescription:\n\nCollecting data is useless unless you use it to make improvements. Today, you will review the results of our class survey and act as a consultant to improve the operation of our league/event.\n\nThe Task:\n\nReview the Google Forms summary charts and responses. Then, write a response addressing the following:\n\n1. The Data (3 Points of Interest)\n\n- Using 100 words (minimum), describe three specific data points from the survey that you find interesting or surprising.\n\n2. The Suggestion (Action Plan)\n\n- Give one concrete suggestion for how our league/event should be organized or operated differently based on this feedback.\n\n3. The Justification (Cite Your Sources)\n\n- You must cite the survey data to justify your suggestion.\n- Protect the Data: Do not include any respondent's name or email in your response. In one sentence, explain why survey data must be kept private.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can solve a problem using data by giving one concrete suggestion for how our league or event should be run differently, based on what the survey feedback shows (required)\n- I can use research to back a marketing decision by citing specific numbers or responses from the survey to justify my suggestion\n- I can protect private information by leaving out every respondent's name and email and explaining in one sentence why survey data must be kept private\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can use math to read survey results by giving counts or percentages from the summary charts when I describe my three interesting findings\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your analysis as a Text Entry.",
    "plan": {
      "duration": "1 Class Period",
      "days": [
        {
          "label": "",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "title": "Warm-up",
              "minutes": 5,
              "mode": "warmup",
              "detail": "If 80% of students say they hate the cafeteria pizza, but the sales data shows it is the #1 selling item, what is the truth?",
              "fixed": true
            },
            {
              "title": "The Hook",
              "minutes": 10,
              "mode": "listen",
              "detail": "Data is just noise until you tell a story with it. You have collected the answers. You have the charts. Now, you have to stop being researchers and start being decision-makers. Use the data to fix the problems.\" Mini-Lesson (Comp 16): Survey answers belong to the people who gave them. Show how to share results without names, keep the form's response sheet restricted, and never post raw responses. "
            },
            {
              "title": "Survey Analysis (Data Driven Decisions)",
              "minutes": null,
              "mode": "devices",
              "detail": "Self-paced: the assignment, on the Student Dashboard."
            },
            {
              "title": "Checkout Slip",
              "minutes": 5,
              "mode": "write",
              "detail": "Why is it safer for a business to make a decision based on data rather than 'gut feeling'?",
              "fixed": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
