    "promptText": "Title: Assignment: The 6-Second Resume\n\nDescription:\n\nRecruiters spend an average of 6 seconds looking at a resume before deciding to keep it or trash it. Your resume must be clean, professional, and easy to read.\n\nThe Task:\n\nCreate a one page professional resume.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Header: Name, Professional Email, Phone Number, LinkedIn URL.\n- Education: School, Graduation Date, GPA.\n- Experience: List any jobs, volunteer work, or club leadership.\n- Skills: List Soft Skills and Hard Skills.\n- The \"Action Verb\" Rule: Every bullet point under your experience must start with an Action Verb.\n- The Target: Find one real job or internship posting on TeamWork Online, Indeed, Handshake or a team's careers page that your resume could be sent to, and paste the link at the bottom.\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can write a professional resume by making a one-page resume with the full header, education, experience bullets that each start with an action verb, and soft and hard skills (required)\n- I can find job search resources by locating one real job or internship posting on TeamWork Online, Indeed, Handshake or a team's careers page and pasting its link\n\nYou can also show:\n\n- I can stay safe online by using a professional email address and sharing only the contact details my resume header asks for\n- I can complete a job application by filling in my school, graduation date, GPA and experience accurately, the same way I would on a real application\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your Resume as a PDF file.",
