    "definitionOfDone": "ASSIGNMENT: L34 INTERVIEW SKILLS PRACTICE PLAN\nCOURSE: 8175 Sports Entertainment and Event Marketing\nCOMPETENCIES ASSESSED: 8175-112, 8175-3\n\nTHE TASK (what the student was asked to do)\nTitle: Assignment: Interview Skills Practice Plan\n\nDescription:\n\nKnowing *what* to say in an interview is only half the battle. *How* you say it—your body language, your tone, and your confidence—matters just as much.\n\nThe Task:\n\n- Watch: Watch the Video on Interview Skills.\n- Plan: Write a 100-word plan to practice these skills prior to an interview opportunity.\n- Reflect:\n\n- What did you learn from the video that was not expected?\n- How did this experience help shape your future career plans?\n- What is something specific you could do that would help you in an interview setting?\n\nWhat your work needs to show:\n\n- I can describe how a job interview works by explaining what surprised me in the interview skills video and naming one specific thing I could do in an interview (required)\n- I can take charge of my own growth by writing a 100-word plan for practicing my body language, tone and confidence on my own before an interview\n\nSubmission:\n\nSubmit your plan as a Text Entry.\n\nPRIMARY COMPETENCY (Milestone 1; must be MET)\n- 8175-112 Describe the job interview process.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * researching the company and the position before the interview\n    * understanding the importance of cultivating industry knowledge\n    * preparing answers to anticipated questions\n    * wearing professional attire\n    * being on time\n    * introducing oneself\n    * making eye contact\n    * listening attentively to the interviewer\n    * maintaining a respectful demeanor\n    * asking questions\n    * speaking clearly\n    * refraining from consuming or carrying food, drink, or gum\n    * refraining from checking one’s phone\n    * writing a follow-up communication (e.g., a thank-you note)\n\nSECONDARY COMPETENCIES (must be at least PARTIALLY MET)\n- 8175-3 Demonstrate initiative and self-direction.\n    Evidence can include (examples, not all required):\n    * recognizing the importance of proactive, independent decision making\n    * identifying workplace needs\n    * completing tasks with minimal direct supervision\n    * applying solutions\n\nTERTIARY COMPETENCIES (never required; name any the work clearly shows under ALSO SHOWN)\n- None for this assignment.\n\nTEACHER GRADING NOTES\nFocus on the \"Plan\" aspect. Did they list specific ways they will practice (e.g., \"I will record myself answering questions\")?\n\nPASSING RULE: APPROVED when Milestone 1 (the primary competency) is MET and Milestones 2, 3 and 4 are each MET or PARTIALLY MET. Tertiary competencies never affect the result.\n\nPASSING STANDARD\nThe work does every part of the task the assignment asks for, in the student's own words. Specific examples, not general statements. Judge each competency only by what this assignment asks the student to do. The lines under a competency are examples of what evidence can look like, not a checklist: one specific, well-done example that fits the task is enough, and a part of a competency the task does not ask for is never required."
